      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When prioritizing long-term social cohesion, data often suggests that predictable legal frameworks enhance societal trust more effectively than purely reactive enforcement. While sovereignty is fundamental, an entirely closed system often leads to shadow economies that undermine rule of law internally. Therefore, a stable model must integrate enhanced sovereignty measures with clear, functioning legal routes that address the demand driving illegal entry in the first place.",
      "source": "target",
